      "id": "claim_be97e3fbbcc945c88158e3da7950bc04",
      "statement": "File compatibility is a reader boundary: celld and Litestream v0.5.16 read both block and frame files while v0.5.11 reads only frames; the ordinary L0 writer still emits frames, the v0.5.2 encoder/compactor emit blocks, and because the node-wide additive L1 scheduler is on by default a mixed fleet must keep CELLD_LTX_COMPACTION=0 until every takeover target can read block files.",
